{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardSYT","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardSYT","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasisCore"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.sytToTableau_colSuperstandardSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.sytToTableau_colSuperstandardSYT","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardSYT.lean#L77-L83","doc":"**The bridge.** Reading `colSuperstandardSYT μ` back through the\nlabel→cell bijection returns the original column-superstandard filling, so every\n`colSuperstandard`-indexed statement transfers verbatim to the SYT-indexed\n`seminormalVector_base_exists`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.colSuperstandardSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.colSuperstandardSYT","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardSYT.lean#L70-L75","doc":"**The column-superstandard tableau, as a `StandardYoungTableau`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.labelAt_col_strict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.labelAt_col_strict","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardSYT.lean#L57-L68","doc":"**Column-strictness.** `(i, j)` and `(i + 1, j)` share column `j`, so the\nfirst disjunct of `lt_iff_colRow` is unavailable and the second one — same\ncolumn, smaller row — gives `i < i + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.labelAt_row_strict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.labelAt_row_strict","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardSYT.lean#L44-L55","doc":"**Row-strictness.** `(i, j)` and `(i, j + 1)` sit in *different* columns, so\n`lt_iff_colRow`'s first disjunct applies and the label order is the column order\n`j < j + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.coe_apply_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ColSuperstandardTableau.coe_apply_symm","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ColSuperstandardSYT.lean#L34-L42","doc":"Reading the column-superstandard filling at the label it assigns to `(i, j)`\nreturns `(i, j)`.  Pure `Equiv.apply_symm_apply`, isolated because the two\nstrictness proofs below each use it twice and the coercion tower\n(`μ.cells → ℕ × ℕ`) makes it awkward inline. ","signatureChunk":0}]}